        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.595,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Parallel and Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.441,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "From this we can observe:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.137,
            0.825,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "When the corresponding angles formed by a transversal on a pair of lines are equal to each other, then the pair of lines are parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.216,
            0.846,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "Suppose, we have a transversal intersecting two parallel lines. What can be said about the corresponding angles?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.263,
            0.259,
            0.285
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.283,
            0.849,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 5.19 has a pair of parallel lines l and m (what is the notation used in the figure to indicate they are parallel?) . Line t is the transversal across these two lines. $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are corresponding angles. Take a tracing paper and trace $\\angle a$ on it. Now place this tracing paper over $\\angle b$ and see if the angles align exactly. You will observe that the angles match. Check the other corresponding angles in the figure using a protractor. Are all the corresponding angles equal to each other?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.417,
            0.6,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.463,
                0.57,
                0.537,
                0.584
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.19"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.611,
            0.824,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "Corresponding angles formed by a transversal intersecting a pair of parallel lines are always equal to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.678,
            0.258,
            0.699
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.697,
            0.847,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "In Fig. 5.20, draw a transversal t to the lines l and m such that one pair of corresponding angles is equal. You can measure the angles with a protractor."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
